EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §4.1, §5.6: baked gen/go writes a literal union as its wire string, so a selected value holding a union over a dependent type whose value is not a string (an enum branch's member) is DependentType at the value; a string value is written.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A color.
enum Color { red, blue }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => String, two => Color }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
  /// Its payload, or none.
  u: P(k) | "none"
}

/// Holds a color.
let colored: Thing = { k: two, u: red }

/// Holds a string.
let named: Thing = { k: one, u: "x" }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- a.colored.json --
{"k": "two", "u": "red"}
-- a.named.json --
{"k": "one", "u": "x"}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:21:5
  emit go in baked mode cannot generate a dependent type

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
